From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: retain separate PHYs for Miami RAM testing

The SDK's MLO path combines firmware radios under one wiphy even when
there is no inter-device WSI group. Miami needs separate AHB 2 GHz and
PCI 5/6 GHz PHYs for the existing native discovery/renderer path. Disable
MLO capability only for this exact machine until separately qualified;
leave the firmware hardware-mode selection and other boards unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -4722,6 +4722,12 @@
 	struct ath12k_base *ab;
 	int i;
 
+	/* Miami's native renderer requires one wiphy per firmware PHY. */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("cambiumnetworks,x7-35x")) {
+		ag->mlo_capable = false;
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (ath12k_ftm_mode || !ath12k_mlo_capable)
 		return;
 
